  "status": "Root cause reproduced in the actual candidate5 shared library and complete-method control. Fixed controls pass; candidate6 full RPM/native regression running. No release qualification claim yet.",
  "source": "deps/v8/src/heap/mark-compact.cc: MarkCompactCollector::CollectEvacuationCandidates",
  "root_cause": "compact_on_every_full_gc makes in_standard_path false, bypassing max_evacuated_bytes, target_fragmentation_percent and free_bytes_threshold initialization. The final selection branch still prints these three variables whenever trace_fragmentation_verbose is true. Candidate5 prints impossible threshold values; the original complete-method control reports 592 Valgrind uses/branches on uninitialized values in formatting.",
  "fix": "In forced mode, log the mode and initialized page/live-byte fields instead of unused heuristics. Standard heuristic output and every candidate-selection statement remain unchanged. No default initialization masking the absent computation and no warning suppression.",
  "coverage": {
    "checks": 153600,
    "configurations": "All 16 mode-flag combinations; tracing off/on; four spaces; empty, single-page and seven-page inputs; pinned, never-evacuated and non-allocatable pages; manual/random/stress/forced selection; exact ordinary/forced trace fields. Debug and optimized Release, normally and under Valgrind.",
    "memory": "Fixed runs: zero errors and all allocations freed. Baseline exposes uninitialized reads.",
    "native_regression": "The real candidate5 RPM library fails the new forced-trace assertion and visibly prints garbage thresholds. New packaged Python test invokes ordinary/standard-trace/forced-trace Node processes, exercising 90,009 retained-value assertions plus trace structure. Fixed native test waits for full candidate6 build."
  },
  "limits": "Complete selection method is unchanged except for the fix. Typed heap/page/sweeper adapters replace runtime objects; deterministic heuristic/random helpers test control flow and selection invariants, not real GC scheduling or heuristic estimation. Actual library regression is separate.",
